  <!-- URL FORM MATCHES WHAT THE SERVER ACTUALLY SERVES.
       Cloudflare Pages serves every prerendered page from dist/<route>/index.html
       at a TRAILING-SLASH url and 308-redirects the no-slash form to it, so these
       carry the slash. SPA routes (/green /tube /feed) are served at the no-slash
       form (200), so they do not. Getting this wrong is what had Google indexing
       /about and /about/ as two pages; the canonical tags (prerender.mjs) now use
       the same trailing-slash form. -->

